			<abstract>
				<p>Convolutional neural network (CNN) inference based on RNS-CKKS enables secure processing on encrypted data but introduces significant weight size overhead. Weight plaintext, weight in RNS-CKKS format, can reach tens to hundreds of gigabytes. Existing compression methods either add high computational cost or yield low compression rates. In this work, we propose WPC, Weight Plaintext Compression, to compress weight plaintext for RNS-CKKS-based CNN inference. We observe that the transformation from the weight in CNN models to the weight plaintext in RNS-CKKS format involves an operation akin to the Discrete Fourier Transform, which shifts data between the time and frequency domains while retaining</p>
			</abstract>
